winemac: a stand-in under the Windows file name, so Discord finds the game

Discord recognises a game on the Mac by the file name of a running app ("endfield.exe",
"zenlesszonezero game/zenlesszonezero.exe"). Found by trying with Discord: it only looks at
processes macOS lists as apps, that are not inside an app bundle, and that have a window. A
program under FineWine runs from a bundle of its own name (patch 0024, for the Dock and Game
Mode), so its Windows file name was never seen and a game showed only as an entry added by
hand.

When a program first shows itself (becomes a regular app), the Mac driver now copies the
runtime's finewine-presence (runtime-extras/presence-helper, built by `package`) to
<prefix>/.finewine-apps/presence/<folder>/<file> and starts it with this process's id. That
program is an app without a Dock icon that owns one clear pixel of window and ends when the
process does. Windows' own programs get none. FINEWINE_GAME_PRESENCE=0 turns it off.

